    style Rep fill:#FFF,stroke:#ffcc5c,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
    style VPR fill:#FFF,stroke:#ffcc5c,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
```





## `VetiverModel` -> `VetiverAPI`

Finally, we'll turn the model into an API. 





```{python}
from vetiver import VetiverAPI
app = VetiverAPI(v, check_prototype = True)
```





**`VetiverAPI()`** creates a production-ready web API that wraps the trained model, validates inputs, and returns predictions via HTTP. 





```{mermaid}
%%| fig-cap: 'VetiverAPI()'
%%| fig-align: center
%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral', 'themeVariables': { 'fontFamily': 'monospace', "fontSize":"16px"}}}%%
flowchart LR
    VetMod["<code>VetiverModel()</code>"] --> VetAPI["<code>VetiverAPI()</code>"]
    VetAPI --> REST["<strong>REST</strong> API<br>Server"]
    REST --> HttpEP["<strong>HTTP</strong><br>Endpoints"]
    
    HttpEP --> Post["<strong>POST</strong><br>/predict"]
    HttpEP --> GetPing["<strong>GET</strong><br>/ping"]
    HttpEP --> GetProto["<strong>GET</strong><br>/prototype"]
    HttpEP --> GetMeta["<strong>GET</strong><br>/metadata"]
    
    style VetMod fill:#FFF,stroke:#4CBB9D,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
    style VetAPI fill:#FFF,stroke:#4CBB9D,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
    style REST fill:#FFF,stroke:#4CBB9D,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
    
    style HttpEP fill:#FFF,stroke:#ff6f69,color:#000,stroke-width:2px,rx:5,ry:5,font-size:15px
    
    style Post fill:#FFF,stroke:#ffcc5c,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
    style GetPing fill:#FFF,stroke:#ffcc5c,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
    style GetProto fill:#FFF,stroke:#ffcc5c,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
    style GetMeta fill:#FFF,stroke:#ffcc5c,color:#000,stroke-width:3px,rx:10,ry:10,font-size:16px
```





This makes our model accessible to any application that can make web requests, which we will cover in the next lab. 
